      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نُدْبَةٌ</span></b> , a subst., <i>A call; a summons; an invitation to do a thing.</i> (Msb.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نُدْبَةٌ</span>: a subst.,
(tropical:)  The <i>act of wailing for, weeping for, lamenting,</i>
or <i>deploring the loss of, one who is dead, as
described in the explanations of</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَدَبَ الميّت</span>, and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَدَبَتْه</span>. (S, K, M, Msb.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  [<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَآءُ النَّدْبَةِ</span> <i>The</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ه</span>
<i>of lamentation</i>]. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَرَبِىٌّ نُدْبَةٌ</span> <i>An Arabian of
chaste speech;</i> (K;) <i>eloquent.</i> (TA.)

